From: Lukas Klizas <lukas@klizas.lt>
Subject: [PATCH] x86/smpboot: don't defer AP cache/MTRR init across S3 resume bringup

On resume from S3, arch_thaw_secondary_cpus_begin() sets
cache_aps_delayed_init, so cache_ap_online() skips cache_cpu_init() for
every secondary CPU. MTRRs are only programmed after the last CPU is up,
in arch_thaw_secondary_cpus_end() -> cache_aps_init().

Until then the APs run with MTRR contents at reset state: MTRRdefType
reads 0xc00 (enabled, default type UC, no variable ranges programmed),
so the effective memory type for all of RAM is UC. Each AP executes its
entire serial bringup — and every tick it services once online — from
uncached memory. Measured on an i9-9880H (MacBookPro16,1): dependent-ALU
loops 500-8000x slower, 8 MB memset at 1.7 MB/s, ~1 ms per empty tick at
HZ=1000. With 11 secondary CPUs the "Enabling non-boot CPUs" phase takes
8-97 s depending on pending tick work; the soft lockup detector fires on
cpuhp with 89% hardirq time. HT siblings of the boot CPU are unaffected
(MTRRs are core-scoped, the sibling sees the boot CPU's live MTRRs and
reads 0xc06) — that asymmetry confirms the mechanism.

Regular hotplug doesn't defer: cache_ap_online() runs the
stop_machine_from_inactive_cpu() rendezvous and the incoming CPU gets
cached before CPUHP_AP_ONLINE. Onlining a CPU that way takes ~25 ms on
the same machine vs seconds on the thaw path.

Drop the deferral and let the thaw path take the regular hotplug route.
The per-AP rendezvous costs a brief pause of the already-online CPUs,
which is noise next to running the bringup uncached.

Signed-off-by: Lukas Klizas <lukas@klizas.lt>
---
 arch/x86/kernel/smpboot.c | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/x86/kernel/smpboot.c b/arch/x86/kernel/smpboot.c
--- a/arch/x86/kernel/smpboot.c
+++ b/arch/x86/kernel/smpboot.c
@@ -1257,13 +1257,11 @@
 
 void arch_thaw_secondary_cpus_begin(void)
 {
-	set_cache_aps_delayed_init(true);
 }
 
 void arch_thaw_secondary_cpus_end(void)
 {
 	clocksource_touch_watchdog();
-	cache_aps_init();
 }
 
